{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally in the UK", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Visit to Covent Garden", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Between the Market Stalls > A Must in London - Covent Garden Market", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about directions to places in a limited range of social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Describing Places with Prepositions of Place", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you describe places, you use prepositions of place like <span class=\"strong\">through, on </span> or <span class=\"strong\"> at.</span> <br><br>You go <span class=\"italic\">through</span>  a space, like a park or a market.<br>You walk <span class=\"italic\">on</span>  a street.<br>You use <span class=\"italic\">at</span>  to talk about a place, like a pub.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can walk through the market.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are jugglers and musicians on every street.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You can have a snack or something to drink at a local pub.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Near, Close, Far", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the adjectives <span class=\"strong\">near</span>, <span class=\"strong\">close</span> and <span class=\"strong\">far</span> to say the distance of one thing or place to another.<br><br><span class=\"italic\">Near</span>  and <span class=\"italic\">close</span>  have the same meaning. <span class=\"italic\">Far</span>  has the opposite meaning. <br><br> The expression <span class=\"italic\">too far</span> means something is very far in a negative way.<br><br>You often talk about how far something is using the time it takes to walk or drive.  A hyphen ( - ) goes between the number and the word <span class=\"italic\">minute</span> or <span class=\"italic\">hour</span>, like  <span class=\"italic\">10-minute drive.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Is the market far? <br> <span class=\"strong\">Tourist Agent</span>: No, it's very close. It's about a 10-minute walk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: How far is the airport? <br><span class=\"strong\">Tourist Agent</span>: It's not far either. It's a 15-minute drive.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "antique", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a very old object", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will find art, antiques, food, and fashion in the market.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you visit a city.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pub ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a bar where you can order food", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can have a snack or something to drink at a local pub.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "atmosphere", "type": "name"}, {"content": "environment; mood of a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's a great spot to experience the London atmosphere.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have a story to tell", "type": "name"}, {"content": "many interesting things have happened", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Every building has a story to tell.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "center ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "most important place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Covent Garden is also the theater center of London.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "juggler ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a performer who throws and catches objects", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are jugglers and musicians on every street.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "walk ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the time it takes to walk to a place ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"},